fragment_downloaded_cb({"url":"codecparsers/gsth266parser.html#GstH266VPS","fragment":"\n\tGstH266VPS\n\nMembers\n\n\tGstCodecParsers.H266VPS\n\nMembers\n\n\tGstCodecParsers.H266VPS\n\nMembers\nStructure defining the H266 VPS.\nprovides an identifier for the VPS for reference by other syntax\nelements.\nspecifies the number of layers specified by the VPS.\nspecifies the maximum number of temporal sublayers\nthat may be present in a layer specified by the VPS.\nspecifies whether the syntax elements\nvps_ptl_max_tid, vps_dpb_max_tid, and vps_hrd_max_tid are present.\nspecifies whether all layers specified by the\nVPS are independently coded without using inter-layer prediction.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the i-th layer.\nspecifies whether the layer with index i does not\nuse inter-layer prediction.\nspecifies whether the syntax element\nvps_max_tid_il_ref_pics_plus1 could be present.\nspecifies whether the layer with index j is not a\ndirect reference layer for the layer with index i.\nspecifies whether the pictures of the j-th layer\nthat are neither IRAP pictures nor GDR pictures with ph_recovery_poc_cnt\nequal to 0 are not used as ILRPs for decoding of pictures of the i-th layer.\nspecifies whether each OLS specified by the VPS\ncontains only one layer and each layer specified by the VPS is an OLS with\nthe single included layer being the only output layer.\nspecifies whether the total number of OLSs specified by the\nVPS is equal to vps_max_layers_minus1 + 1.\nspecifies the total number of OLSs specified by the VPS.\nspecifies the number of multi-layer OLSs (i.e., OLSs\nthat contain more than one layer).\nspecifies the index to the list of multi-layer OLSs\nfor the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of layers in the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the j-th layer in\nthe i-th OLS.\nspecifies the total number of OLSs\nspecified by the VPS when vps_ols_mode_idc is equal to 2.\nspecifies whether the layer with nuh_layer_id\nequal to vps_layer_id[j] is an output layer of the i-th OLS when\nvps_ols_mode_idc is equal to 2.\nspecifies the number of output layers in\nthe i-th OLS.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the j-th\noutput layer in the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of sublayers in the\nj-th layer in the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of profile_tier_level\nsyntax structures in the VPS.\nspecifies whether profile, tier, and general constraints\ninformation are present in the i-th profile_tier_level syntax structure\nin the VPS.\nspecifies the TemporalId of the highest sublayer representation.\nspecifies the profile, tier and level using\nGstH266ProfileTierLevel.\nspecifies the index of the profile_tier_level syntax\nstructure that applies to the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of dpb_parameters syntax\nstrutcures in the VPS.\nis used to control the presence of\ndpb_max_dec_pic_buffering_minus1[j], dpb_max_num_reorder_pics[j], and\ndpb_max_latency_increase_plus1[j] syntax elements in the dpb_parameters\nsyntax strucures in the VPS.\nspecifies the TemporalId of the highest sublayer representation\nfor which the DPB parameters could be present in the i-th dpb_parameters\nsyntax strutcure in the VPS.\nthe DPB parameters using GstH266DPBParameters.\nspecifies the width of each picture storage buffer for\nthe i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies the height of each picture storage buffer\nfor the i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies the greatest allowed value of\nsps_chroma_format_idc for all SPSs.\nspecifies the greatest allowed value of\nsps_bitdepth_minus8 for all SPSs.\nspecifies the index of the dpb_parameters syntax\nstructure that applies to the i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies whether the VPS contains a\ngeneral_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structure and other HRD parameters.\nHRD parameters in GstH266GeneralHRDParameters.\nspecifies that the i-th\nols_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structure in the VPS contains HRD\nparameters for the sublayer representations.\nspecifies the number of\nols_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structures present in the VPS.\nspecifies the TemporalId of the highest sublayer representation\nfor which the HRD parameters are contained in the i-th\nols_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structure.\nOLS HRD parameters using GstH266OLSHRDParameters.\nspecifies the index of the ols_timing_hrd_parameters\nsyntax structure that applies to the i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies whether no vps_extension_data_flag syntax elements\nare present in the VPS RBSP syntax structure.\ncould have any value, it is not defined in this version of\nthis Specification.\nwhether this VPS is valid.\n\n\tSince\t\t\t: 1.26\n\t\t\nStructure defining the H266 VPS.\nprovides an identifier for the VPS for reference by other syntax\nelements.\nspecifies the number of layers specified by the VPS.\nspecifies the maximum number of temporal sublayers\nthat may be present in a layer specified by the VPS.\nspecifies whether the syntax elements\nvps_ptl_max_tid, vps_dpb_max_tid, and vps_hrd_max_tid are present.\nspecifies whether all layers specified by the\nVPS are independently coded without using inter-layer prediction.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the i-th layer.\nspecifies whether the layer with index i does not\nuse inter-layer prediction.\nspecifies whether the syntax element\nvps_max_tid_il_ref_pics_plus1 could be present.\nspecifies whether the layer with index j is not a\ndirect reference layer for the layer with index i.\nspecifies whether the pictures of the j-th layer\nthat are neither IRAP pictures nor GDR pictures with ph_recovery_poc_cnt\nequal to 0 are not used as ILRPs for decoding of pictures of the i-th layer.\nspecifies whether each OLS specified by the VPS\ncontains only one layer and each layer specified by the VPS is an OLS with\nthe single included layer being the only output layer.\nspecifies whether the total number of OLSs specified by the\nVPS is equal to vps_max_layers_minus1 + 1.\nspecifies the total number of OLSs specified by the VPS.\nspecifies the number of multi-layer OLSs (i.e., OLSs\nthat contain more than one layer).\nspecifies the index to the list of multi-layer OLSs\nfor the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of layers in the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the j-th layer in\nthe i-th OLS.\nspecifies the total number of OLSs\nspecified by the VPS when vps_ols_mode_idc is equal to 2.\nspecifies whether the layer with nuh_layer_id\nequal to vps_layer_id[j] is an output layer of the i-th OLS when\nvps_ols_mode_idc is equal to 2.\nspecifies the number of output layers in\nthe i-th OLS.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the j-th\noutput layer in the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of sublayers in the\nj-th layer in the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of profile_tier_level\nsyntax structures in the VPS.\nspecifies whether profile, tier, and general constraints\ninformation are present in the i-th profile_tier_level syntax structure\nin the VPS.\nspecifies the TemporalId of the highest sublayer representation.\nspecifies the profile, tier and level using\nGstCodecParsers.H266ProfileTierLevel.\nspecifies the index of the profile_tier_level syntax\nstructure that applies to the i-th OLS.\nspecifies the number of dpb_parameters syntax\nstrutcures in the VPS.\nis used to control the presence of\ndpb_max_dec_pic_buffering_minus1[j], dpb_max_num_reorder_pics[j], and\ndpb_max_latency_increase_plus1[j] syntax elements in the dpb_parameters\nsyntax strucures in the VPS.\nspecifies the TemporalId of the highest sublayer representation\nfor which the DPB parameters could be present in the i-th dpb_parameters\nsyntax strutcure in the VPS.\nthe DPB parameters using GstCodecParsers.H266DPBParameters.\nspecifies the width of each picture storage buffer for\nthe i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies the height of each picture storage buffer\nfor the i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies the greatest allowed value of\nsps_chroma_format_idc for all SPSs.\nspecifies the greatest allowed value of\nsps_bitdepth_minus8 for all SPSs.\nspecifies the index of the dpb_parameters syntax\nstructure that applies to the i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies whether the VPS contains a\ngeneral_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structure and other HRD parameters.\nHRD parameters in GstCodecParsers.H266GeneralHRDParameters.\nspecifies that the i-th\nols_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structure in the VPS contains HRD\nparameters for the sublayer representations.\nspecifies the number of\nols_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structures present in the VPS.\nspecifies the TemporalId of the highest sublayer representation\nfor which the HRD parameters are contained in the i-th\nols_timing_hrd_parameters syntax structure.\nOLS HRD parameters using GstCodecParsers.H266OLSHRDParameters.\nspecifies the index of the ols_timing_hrd_parameters\nsyntax structure that applies to the i-th multi-layer OLS.\nspecifies whether no vps_extension_data_flag syntax elements\nare present in the VPS RBSP syntax structure.\ncould have any value, it is not defined in this version of\nthis Specification.\nwhether this VPS is valid.\n\n\tSince\t\t\t: 1.26\n\t\t\nStructure defining the H266 VPS.\nprovides an identifier for the VPS for reference by other syntax\nelements.\nspecifies the number of layers specified by the VPS.\nspecifies the maximum number of temporal sublayers\nthat may be present in a layer specified by the VPS.\nspecifies whether the syntax elements\nvps_ptl_max_tid, vps_dpb_max_tid, and vps_hrd_max_tid are present.\nspecifies whether all layers specified by the\nVPS are independently coded without using inter-layer prediction.\nspecifies the nuh_layer_id value of the i-th layer.\nspecifies whether the layer with index i does not\nuse inter-layer prediction.\nspecifies whether the syntax element\nvps_max_tid_il_ref_pics_plus1 could be present.\nspecifies whether the layer with index j is not a\ndirect reference layer for the layer with index i.\nspecifies whether the pictures of the j-th layer\nthat are neither IRAP pictures no